\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#experimental}{\figure{lifecycle-experimental.svg}{options: alt='[Experimental]'}}}{\strong{[Experimental]}}

\code{wjp_upset()} draws an UpSet chart, the alternative to Venn diagrams for
many overlapping sets: one bar per intersection of sets (e.g., the unmet
needs that people report together), a matrix of dots below the bars that
shows which sets form each intersection, and the size of every set as a
horizontal bar on the left. Unlike \code{ComplexUpset}, which returns a
patchwork of several plots, \code{wjp_upset()} returns a single ggplot, so the
WJP theme, fonts, and \code{\link[=wjp_drawn]{wjp_drawn()}} apply to the whole chart.
}
\details{
