\code{"Access to Assistance + Access to Information"}, or a list column of
character vectors), its value in \code{target}, and optionally its printed value
in \code{labels}. Intersections are drawn from left to right in the order of the
data, or of the \code{order} column.

Sets are listed from top to bottom in the order of \code{sets}: a character
vector of set names, or a data frame whose first column holds the set names
and whose \code{set_target} and \code{set_labels} columns hold their sizes and
printed sizes. When the sizes are not given, a set's size is the sum of the
values of the intersections that contain it, and no size label is printed.

The chart is drawn on a canvas of \code{width} by \code{height} points (the panel of
intersection bars on the upper \code{bar_ratio} of the plotting height, the
matrix below it, and the set sizes on the left), so \code{\link[=wjp_save]{wjp_save()}} writes it
at that exact size. Each intersection bar is 0.9 of its column, as tall as
its value relative to the largest value times \code{bar_headroom}.
